{
  "id": "11424_boumei",
  "headword": "{亡命|ぼうめい}",
  "reading": "ぼうめい",
  "part_of_speech": "noun / suru verb",
  "gloss": "exile, defection, seeking asylum",
  "schema_version": "2.0",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "exile, defection, seeking asylum",
      "explanation": "Fleeing one's own country for political reasons and seeking refuge in another country. Also refers to the state of living in exile."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "11424_boumei_ex1",
      "japanese": "{彼|かれ}は{海外|かいがい}に{亡命|ぼうめい}した。",
      "english": "He went into exile abroad.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "11424_boumei_ex2",
      "japanese": "{政治的|せいじてき}な{理由|りゆう}で{亡命|ぼうめい}を{求|もと}めた。",
      "english": "He sought asylum for political reasons.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "11424_boumei_ex3",
      "japanese": "{独裁|どくさい}{政権|せいけん}から{逃|のが}れるために{多|おお}くの{知識人|ちしきじん}が{隣国|りんこく}に{亡命|ぼうめい}した。",
      "english": "Many intellectuals defected to neighboring countries to escape the dictatorship.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "COMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {亡命|ぼうめい}する (to go into exile, to defect)\n- {亡命|ぼうめい}{者|しゃ} (exile, defector, refugee)\n- {亡命|ぼうめい}{政府|せいふ} (government in exile)\n- {亡命|ぼうめい}を{求|もと}める (to seek asylum)\n- {政治|せいじ}{亡命|ぼうめい} (political exile)\n\nThe characters literally mean \"{亡|ぼう}\" (to flee/perish) + \"{命|めい}\" (life/fate), conveying the sense of fleeing to save one's life.",
